physical.summary:
Postcard (black and white with colour); a Navajo silversmith, Dah Pah, sitting on the ground in a hogan, working silver at an anvil; he wears Navajo-style clothing and ornament, including a cloth wrap around his head and a squash blossom necklace; he is surrounded by smithing tools; 
Coolidge, New Mexico, USA.
Printed

